# Root .gitignore.
#
# There was none until 2026-08-14, so the repository-root `logs/` directory was **tracked**: 17 runtime log
# files, dirtied by every test run, and past commits swept 852 lines of log churn into the history.
#
# That matters more here than it would elsewhere. RFC 9700 §4.2.4 (T0-1) was a finding about credentials
# reaching `logs/app-*.log` — client secrets, ROPC passwords, authorization codes, PKCE verifiers, refresh
# tokens — so committing that directory is the same defect one layer out. The tracked files were scanned
# when this was added and contained no credential-shaped strings, which is evidence that T0-1's fix holds;
# it is not a reason to keep committing them.
#
# `server/.gitignore` has ignored `server/logs/*` from the start. This is the sibling that was missing.
logs/*
!logs/.gitkeep

# `node_modules/` has been listed here since this file was created — and it did not help, because
# **.gitignore has no effect on a file already in the index.** One file slipped in before this file
# existed and stayed tracked for four days despite the rule directly above it:
# `node_modules/.vite/vitest/da39a3ee.../results.json`, a Vitest run cache, committed in 6eed35a and
# fc63704 on 2026-08-13. `git check-ignore` reported it as **not ignored**, which is the tell.
#
# It came from running `vitest` at the **repo root** rather than in `server/` or `client/` — there is no
# root `package.json` and no root Vitest config, so Vitest resolved no config at all (hence the cache
# directory named `da39a3ee…`, the SHA-1 of the empty string) and globbed both packages' tests into one
# results file. Most entries recorded `failed: true` because nothing resolved without each package's own
# config. Untracked and deleted 2026-08-17.
#
# The lesson is the same one the `logs/` note above records, one layer out: adding the rule was step one,
# and `git rm --cached` was the step that actually removed it. Run the tests with
# `npm --prefix server run test` / `npm --prefix client run test`, never bare `vitest` at the root.
node_modules/
dist/
coverage/

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.DS_Store
*.log
